---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="transcript">

          <p>
            The conversation is a timeline of turns: your messages, the agent's text, collapsible thinking blocks, tool calls with their status and error cards, and a per-turn summary of how many tools ran. Long transcripts stay responsive because rows are measured and reconciled rather than redrawn, and markdown and syntax highlighting are done off the main thread.
          </p>
          <h3>Comment on a line</h3>
          <p>
            Click a line inside a code block or a diff in the conversation and attach a comment to it. The comment is carried into your next prompt as context, so "this branch is wrong" is tied to the exact line instead of described in prose. Annotations stay on the block until you send.
          </p>
          <h3>The todo dock</h3>
          <p>
            While the agent works through a multi-step task, its plan sits as a live checklist above the composer, so the step in progress and the ones still outstanding are visible without scrolling the transcript.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
